ParameterCallouts lays a system's design parameters on its own equipment drawing, with leader lines from numbered labels to the part each one is about.

- Data: a `spec` block with `"as": "callouts"` on a page that has a drawing (`ART` in `assets/src/parts/Hero.js`). A row becomes a callout when it has `at: [x, y]`, the point on the drawing in percent of the square drawing box (0–100, the drawing is fitted with `contain`), and sits inside the `fold`. Up to three per side; a point left of the middle goes left. Every other row, folded ones included, follows as a normal SpecTable underneath ("Show 5 more parameters" when all of them are folded). Renderer: `wCallouts` in `assets/src/blocks/spec.js`; without a drawing or any `at` it renders a plain SpecTable.
- Markup: `.aq-parameter-callouts` > `.aq-parameter-callouts__fig` (`svg.aq-parameter-callouts__leaders`, `aria-hidden`; `.aq-parameter-callouts__art` with the Illustration span, `role="img"` and the page's `ART` label, and `aria-hidden` `.aq-parameter-callouts__pin` numbers; `ol.aq-parameter-callouts__list` of `li.aq-parameter-callouts__item.is-l|is-r[.is-up]`: `.aq-index`, `h3` parameter, value, basis), then the SpecTable.
- The same leader approach as the Hero figure, at section scale: a 2:1 box (viewBox 200 × 100), labels in the outer quarters on a 1 px `flow` rule (the lowest label of a side stands on its rule), `flow` leaders from the rule's inner end to the pin. Labels on a side run top to bottom in the order of their points, so leaders never cross on one side; numbers follow reading order (left column, then right). Pins are `flow`-outlined mono chips (12 px, `radius-sm`) on `surface`. The drawing sits on the plain section ground: no grid, no frame. Each label: the shared index, the parameter in Geist 500 14/20 `ink` (sentence case), the value in Geist Mono 16/22, the basis in Geist 13/18 `ink-muted`.
- Ground: the section's own `surface`, in either theme; tokens only, so it reads in light and dark.
- Phones: the drawing runs full width into the section gutters as a square (about 375 px), with pins at 13 px mono in a 32 px chip; the numbered list below as SpecTable phone rows (parameter in Geist 16/24, then value · basis), each row led by the same `flow`-outlined chip as its pin so the two visibly connect.
- Choose points on the part the row is about (vessels for capacity, the EDI stack for sanitization through EDI, the pump for product-contact finish). If a row names nothing you can point at, leave it without `at`: it lists below. Never add a callout for a part the drawing does not show.

## Motion

Motion (`motion.js`): the drawing prints in bottom to top, the numbered pins strike onto it in order, then each leader draws from its pin out to its callout, the callout's rule runs on, the parameter name follows and the value lands last (wiped left to right). About 3.5 s, once. The phone has no leaders: the pins strike, then the numbered list follows, each value fading in after its name. The spec rows under the figure keep the generic row stagger.
